                            Module = "complete-words",
                            Position = 6,
                            PublicationStatus = 2,
                            Text = "A glacier can move so slowly that its motion is difficult to notice. Scientists {{1}} markers {{2}} frozen {{3}} and {{4}} their {{5}} each {{6}} while {{7}} images {{8}} broader {{9}} over {{10}} periods. Measurements from several years help distinguish a brief seasonal change from a lasting trend. A single photograph cannot show how quickly the ice is moving. Researchers also record snowfall because fresh snow may hide the markers. Combining ground observations with images from above gives a more useful account of the glacier than either method alone.",
